Full source page and relevant shared context inspected. Processes P1 and P2 use shared Boolean variables S1,S2 whose initial values are assigned randomly. Whenever they need their critical sections they execute:
P1: while (S1==S2); critical section; S1=S2;
P2: while (S1!=S2); critical section; S2=not(S1);
Which properties are achieved?
Options: (A) Mutual exclusion but not progress; (B) Progress but not mutual exclusion; (C) Neither mutual exclusion nor progress; (D) Both mutual exclusion and progress. Method: Prove boolean strict-alternation exclusion but lack of progress
